"use strict";(Array.isArray(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs)?self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs:self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=[]).push([[1920],{10251(e,t,o){e.exports=o.p+"assets/img/sellercentral.3018655f.webp"},30810(e,t,o){o.r(t),o.d(t,{comp:()=>h,data:()=>f});var i=o(20641);const a=o.p+"assets/img/Registration.55b2981a.webp",n=o.p+"assets/img/seller-login.c9adcb56.webp",r=o.p+"assets/img/vendor-menu.7f7b1ec0.webp";var l=o(10251);const s=o.p+"assets/img/sellercentral-registration-form.0bc9fa47.webp",d=o.p+"assets/img/seller-registration-page.a0d48df1.webp",c=o.p+"assets/img/registration-details.b6a1bcb6.webp",g=o.p+"assets/img/register-as-vendor.cb3da566.webp",p=o.p+"assets/img/customer-account-become-vendor.2a5f5b57.webp",m={class:"hint-container tip"},u={},h=(0,o(66262).A)(u,[["render",function(e,t){const o=(0,i.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,i.uX)(),(0,i.CE)("div",null,[t[6]||(t[6]=(0,i.Fv)('<h1 id="vendor-registration-process" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-registration-process"><span>Vendor Registration Process</span></a></h1><p>Vendors can register on the marketplace using multiple methods provided by the WooCommerce Marketplace plugin.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/Registration.webp"><img src="'+a+'" alt="Vendor Registration"></a></p><hr><h2 id="method-1-registration-via-vendor-menu" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#method-1-registration-via-vendor-menu"><span>Method 1: Registration via Vendor Menu</span></a></h2><ul><li><p>Vendor clicks on the <strong>Vendor</strong> menu item.</p></li><li><p>The page displays two options:</p><ul><li><strong>Login Here</strong></li><li><strong>Register</strong></li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-login.webp"><img src="'+n+'" alt="Vendor Menu"></a></p></li><li><p>Clicking <strong>Login Here</strong> redirects to the vendor login page.</p></li><li><p>Clicking <strong>Register</strong> redirects to the vendor registration page.</p></li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/vendor-menu.webp"><img src="'+r+'" alt="Vendor Menu"></a></p><hr><h2 id="method-2-registration-via-seller-central-page" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#method-2-registration-via-seller-central-page"><span>Method 2: Registration via Seller Central Page</span></a></h2><ul><li>Vendor visits the <strong>Seller Central</strong> page.</li><li>Clicks on the <strong>Become a Seller</strong> button.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/sellercentral.webp"><img src="'+l+'" alt="Seller Central"></a></p><ul><li>The vendor registration form opens.</li><li>Vendor completes and submits the registration form.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/sellercentral-registration-form.webp"><img src="'+s+'" alt="Seller Central Registration Form"></a></p><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Dedicated Onboarding Endpoint</p><p>Vendors can also access the dedicated onboarding registration portal directly using the clean storefront endpoint:</p><div class="language-text line-numbers-mode" data-highlighter="prismjs" data-ext="text"><pre><code><span class="line">https://your-domain.com/sellercentral/become-vendor/</span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><div class="line-numbers" aria-hidden="true" style="counter-reset:line-number 0;"><div class="line-number"></div></div></div><p>This dedicated page presents the complete vendor onboarding form with password confirmation, live store URL check, and KYC document uploads.</p></div><hr><h2 id="method-3-registration-via-my-account-page" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#method-3-registration-via-my-account-page"><span>Method 3: Registration via My Account Page</span></a></h2><p>If the admin enables <strong>Allow Vendor Registration on My Account</strong>:</p><ul><li>A <strong>vendor registration option</strong> is available on the <strong>My Account</strong> sign-up page.</li><li>The user selects the <strong>“I am a Vendor”</strong> radio button during registration.</li><li>Additional <strong>vendor-specific registration fields</strong> are displayed automatically.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/seller-registration-page.webp"><img src="'+d+'" alt="Seller Registration Page"></a></p><hr><h2 id="vendor-registration-form-fields" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-registration-form-fields"><span>Vendor Registration Form Fields</span></a></h2><p>The vendor must enter the following details:</p><ul><li>Email Address</li><li>Password</li><li>First Name</li><li>Last Name</li><li>Shop Name</li><li>Shop URL</li><li>Phone Number</li><li>Accept Terms &amp; Conditions</li></ul><p>After entering the details, click the <strong>Register</strong> button.</p><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/registration-details.webp"><img src="'+c+'" alt="Registration Details"></a></p><h3 id="additional-registration-form-fields-kyc-verification" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#additional-registration-form-fields-kyc-verification"><span>Additional Registration Form Fields &amp; KYC Verification</span></a></h3><p>Depending on your marketplace configuration, the registration form also includes:</p><ul><li><strong>Confirm Password</strong>: Ensures the applicant enters their password accurately during sign-up.</li><li><strong>KYC Document Type</strong>: If KYC verification is enabled, applicants select their document type from a dropdown menu (e.g., <em>Business License</em>, <em>Government ID</em>, or <em>Utility Bill</em>).</li><li><strong>KYC Document Upload</strong>: An optional or mandatory file upload field supporting common file formats (<em>PDF</em>, <em>JPG</em>, <em>JPEG</em>, <em>PNG</em>, <em>WEBP</em>) within configured file size limits.</li><li><strong>Terms &amp; Conditions Agreement</strong>: When a Terms &amp; Conditions page is selected in admin settings, a checkbox prompt (<code>I have read and agree to the vendor signup terms and conditions</code>) is required before form submission.</li></ul>',28)),(0,i.Lk)("div",m,[t[5]||(t[5]=(0,i.Lk)("p",{class:"hint-container-title"},"Customizing Registration Form Attributes & Labels",-1)),(0,i.Lk)("p",null,[t[2]||(t[2]=(0,i.eW)("Admins can easily customize registration form subtitles, field labels, placeholder texts, and call-to-action button text without touching any code. For full details on all registration attributes and landing page settings, please visit the ")),(0,i.bF)(o,{to:"/documentation/configuration-seller-central.html#registration-section"},{default:(0,i.k6)(()=>t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,i.eW)("Configuration – Seller Central")])),_:1}),t[3]||(t[3]=(0,i.eW)(" documentation page ")),(0,i.bF)(o,{to:"/documentation/configuration-seller-central.html#registration-section"},{default:(0,i.k6)(()=>t[1]||(t[1]=[(0,i.eW)("here")])),_:1}),t[4]||(t[4]=(0,i.eW)("."))])]),t[7]||(t[7]=(0,i.Fv)('<hr><h2 id="shop-url-availability-check" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#shop-url-availability-check"><span>Shop URL Availability Check</span></a></h2><ul><li>The <strong>Shop URL</strong> field uses an <strong>AJAX-based availability check</strong>.</li><li>Displays <strong>“Available”</strong> if the URL is unused.</li><li>Displays <strong>“Already Exists”</strong> if the URL already exists.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/registration-details.webp"><img src="'+c+'" alt="Shop URL Availability"></a></p><h3 id="real-time-validation-feedback" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#real-time-validation-feedback"><span>Real-Time Validation Feedback</span></a></h3><p>When the vendor types a shop slug into the <strong>Shop URL</strong> input field, the marketplace performs an instant real-time AJAX check:</p><ul><li><strong>If the slug is free</strong>: Displays <code>This shop URl is available, kindly proceed.</code> in green confirmation text.</li><li><strong>If the slug is already registered</strong>: Displays <code>This shop URl already EXISTS, please try different shop url.</code> in warning text.</li></ul><div class="hint-container tip"><p class="hint-container-title">Automatic Fallback for Shop Name &amp; Slug</p><p>If the marketplace admin sets <strong>Shop Name on Registration</strong> or <strong>Shop Slug on Registration</strong> to <em>Optional</em> or <em>Remove</em>, applicants do not need to choose a URL manually. The plugin automatically generates a clean URL slug using the vendor&#39;s registered username or shop name.</p></div><hr><h2 id="registration-using-email-password" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#registration-using-email-password"><span>Registration Using Email &amp; Password</span></a></h2><ul><li>Vendor registration is completed using <strong>email and password</strong>.</li><li>Vendor access is granted based on admin approval settings.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/register-as-vendor.webp"><img src="'+g+'" alt="Register as Vendor"></a></p><hr><h2 id="become-a-vendor-from-customer-account" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#become-a-vendor-from-customer-account"><span>Become a Vendor from Customer Account</span></a></h2><ul><li>Existing customers can upgrade to a vendor account.</li><li>A <strong>Become a Vendor</strong> option is available in the <strong>My Account</strong> panel.</li><li>Clicking it initiates the vendor registration process.</li></ul><p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/customer-account-become-vendor.webp"><img src="'+p+'" alt="Become Vendor from Account"></a></p><h3 id="customer-to-vendor-upgrade-experience" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#customer-to-vendor-upgrade-experience"><span>Customer-to-Vendor Upgrade Experience</span></a></h3><p>When registered customers want to sell products on your marketplace:</p><ol><li>The customer logs into their <strong>My Account</strong> dashboard (<code>/my-account/</code>).</li><li>A prominent <strong>Become a Vendor</strong> banner card invites them to register as a seller with the message: <blockquote><p><em>&quot;Submit the request form in the next step and get approval to list and sell your products.&quot;</em></p></blockquote></li><li>Clicking <strong>Become a Vendor</strong> opens the vendor registration form with the customer&#39;s existing name and email address already filled in.</li><li>The customer provides their <strong>Shop Name</strong>, <strong>Shop URL</strong>, contact telephone number, and optional KYC documents.</li><li>All previous customer purchase history, billing addresses, and order details are safely retained while adding vendor capabilities to the account.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="admin-settings-controlling-vendor-registration" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-settings-controlling-vendor-registration"><span>Admin Settings Controlling Vendor Registration</span></a></h2><p>Marketplace administrators have full control over the vendor sign-up experience. These settings are located in the WordPress Admin dashboard under:</p><p><strong>Marketplace &gt; Settings &gt; General</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Setting Label</th><th style="text-align:left;">Type</th><th style="text-align:left;">Options / Values</th><th style="text-align:left;">How It Affects Registration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Allow Vendor Registration on My Account</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox</td><td style="text-align:left;">Enabled / Disabled</td><td style="text-align:left;">When enabled, adds the <strong>I am a Vendor</strong> radio button to the standard WooCommerce My Account registration form. When disabled, vendor signups only occur through Seller Central or the Become Vendor endpoint.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Shop Name on Registration</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Dropdown</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>Required</code>, <code>Optional</code>, <code>Remove</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Controls whether applicants must enter a store name. If set to <em>Remove</em> or left empty, the marketplace automatically uses the vendor&#39;s user name.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Shop Slug on Registration</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Dropdown</td><td style="text-align:left;"><code>Required</code>, <code>Optional</code>, <code>Remove</code></td><td style="text-align:left;">Controls whether the public store URL slug is mandatory. If removed or empty, the system automatically uses the vendor&#39;s username as the shop URL slug.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Auto Approve Vendor</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox</td><td style="text-align:left;">Enabled / Disabled</td><td style="text-align:left;">If checked, newly registered vendors are automatically approved and can access their seller dashboard immediately. If unchecked, new registrations remain pending until manual admin approval.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Vendor Terms &amp; Condition Page</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Dropdown</td><td style="text-align:left;">Page Selector</td><td style="text-align:left;">Selects a published WordPress page for marketplace vendor terms. When set, a mandatory agreement checkbox appears on the registration form.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Enable Vendor KYC Verification</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox</td><td style="text-align:left;">Enabled / Disabled</td><td style="text-align:left;">Adds KYC document type selection and document upload fields directly to the vendor registration form.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>KYC Document Types</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Multi-Select</td><td style="text-align:left;">Business License, Government ID, Utility Bill</td><td style="text-align:left;">Configures which verification document options applicants can select during registration.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Allowed KYC Formats</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Checkbox Group</td><td style="text-align:left;">PDF, JPG, JPEG, PNG, WEBP</td><td style="text-align:left;">Defines the permitted document file extensions for vendor uploads.</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Restrict KYC Document Size</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Number Input</td><td style="text-align:left;">Max Size in KB</td><td style="text-align:left;">Sets maximum file upload limits to prevent large files from slowing down the server.</td></tr></tbody></table><hr><h2 id="vendor-account-approval-workflow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#vendor-account-approval-workflow"><span>Vendor Account Approval Workflow</span></a></h2><p>Once a vendor submits the registration form, the account follows one of two approval workflows depending on the <strong>Auto Approve Vendor</strong> setting:</p><table><thead><tr><th style="text-align:left;">Workflow Stage</th><th style="text-align:left;">Instant Approval Flow (<code>Auto Approve = ON</code>)</th><th style="text-align:left;">Manual Review Flow (<code>Auto Approve = OFF</code>)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Initial Status</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Active / Approved Immediately</td><td style="text-align:left;">Pending Review</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>On-Screen Confirmation</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;"><em>&quot;Congratulations!! Your request has been accepted. Now you are a vendor on the site...&quot;</em></td><td style="text-align:left;"><em>&quot;Your request has been successfully sent to Administrator. You will be notified via Email once it is processed.&quot;</em></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Admin Action Needed</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">None (Automated)</td><td style="text-align:left;">Administrator manual review and approval under <strong>Users &gt; All Users</strong></td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Vendor Access</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Immediate redirection to the <strong>Seller Dashboard</strong> (<code>/seller/vendor-dashboard/</code>)</td><td style="text-align:left;">Login restricted until approved by email notification</td></tr><tr><td style="text-align:left;"><strong>Email Triggers</strong></td><td style="text-align:left;">Welcome / Activation email sent to vendor</td><td style="text-align:left;">Notification sent to Admin (<code>New Vendor Request</code>), followed by approval email to vendor upon activation</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_1-instant-approval-flow-auto-approve-enabled" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-instant-approval-flow-auto-approve-enabled"><span>1. Instant Approval Flow (Auto Approve Enabled)</span></a></h3><ul><li>The vendor account is activated immediately upon submission.</li><li>A confirmation notice appears: <blockquote><p><em>&quot;Congratulations!! Your request has been accepted. Now you are a vendor on the site. You will be redirected to your vendor dashboard soon...&quot;</em></p></blockquote></li><li>The vendor is automatically logged in and redirected to their <strong>Seller Dashboard</strong> (<code>/seller/vendor-dashboard/</code>).</li></ul><h3 id="_2-manual-review-flow-auto-approve-disabled" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-manual-review-flow-auto-approve-disabled"><span>2. Manual Review Flow (Auto Approve Disabled)</span></a></h3><ul><li>The vendor account is placed into a pending status.</li><li>A notice is displayed to the applicant: <blockquote><p><em>&quot;Your request has been successfully sent to Administrator. You will be notified via Email once it is processed.&quot;</em></p></blockquote></li><li>Marketplace administrators receive an email notification (<code>New Vendor Request</code>) and can approve or decline the vendor under <strong>Users &gt; All Users</strong> (filtered by the <code>Seller</code> role).</li><li>Once approved by the admin, the vendor receives an approval email and can log in to access the seller panel.</li></ul>',32))])}]]),f=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/vendor-registration-process.html","title":"Vendor Registration Process","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Vendor Registration Process","description":"Complete step-by-step user guide for vendor registration in the WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace plugin. Learn registration methods, form fields, shop URL check, KYC verification, admin settings, and account approval.","head":[["meta",{"name":"keywords","content":"woocommerce vendor registration, marketplace seller registration, become a seller woocommerce, vendor onboarding flow, seller central registration, vendor kyc verification, marketplace vendor approval"}],["meta",{"property":"og:title","content":"Vendor Registration Process | WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace"}],["meta",{"property":"og:description","content":"Complete step-by-step user guide for vendor registration in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace."}],["meta",{"property":"og:type","content":"article"}]]},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"Method 1: Registration via Vendor Menu","slug":"method-1-registration-via-vendor-menu","link":"#method-1-registration-via-vendor-menu","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Method 2: Registration via Seller Central Page","slug":"method-2-registration-via-seller-central-page","link":"#method-2-registration-via-seller-central-page","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Method 3: Registration via My Account Page","slug":"method-3-registration-via-my-account-page","link":"#method-3-registration-via-my-account-page","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Vendor Registration Form Fields","slug":"vendor-registration-form-fields","link":"#vendor-registration-form-fields","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Additional Registration Form Fields & KYC Verification","slug":"additional-registration-form-fields-kyc-verification","link":"#additional-registration-form-fields-kyc-verification","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Shop URL Availability Check","slug":"shop-url-availability-check","link":"#shop-url-availability-check","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Real-Time Validation Feedback","slug":"real-time-validation-feedback","link":"#real-time-validation-feedback","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Registration Using Email & Password","slug":"registration-using-email-password","link":"#registration-using-email-password","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Become a Vendor from Customer Account","slug":"become-a-vendor-from-customer-account","link":"#become-a-vendor-from-customer-account","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Customer-to-Vendor Upgrade Experience","slug":"customer-to-vendor-upgrade-experience","link":"#customer-to-vendor-upgrade-experience","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Admin Settings Controlling Vendor Registration","slug":"admin-settings-controlling-vendor-registration","link":"#admin-settings-controlling-vendor-registration","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Vendor Account Approval Workflow","slug":"vendor-account-approval-workflow","link":"#vendor-account-approval-workflow","children":[{"level":3,"title":"1. Instant Approval Flow (Auto Approve Enabled)","slug":"_1-instant-approval-flow-auto-approve-enabled","link":"#_1-instant-approval-flow-auto-approve-enabled","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"2. Manual Review Flow (Auto Approve Disabled)","slug":"_2-manual-review-flow-auto-approve-disabled","link":"#_2-manual-review-flow-auto-approve-disabled","children":[]}]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/vendor-registration-process.md"}')}}]);